# HELP xpf_userspace_cos_waterfill_min_epochs_per_worker Minimum waterfill_epochs across workers/bindings WITH active exact-guarantee backlog on this CoS interface. A worker/binding locked in Phase-2 keeps its epochs frozen, dropping this MIN even while the summed epochs climb; a value of 0 is a hard lock-in (a backlogged binding that completed zero epochs). The gauge is SUPPRESSED (no series) for an idle interface with no active-backlog candidate, so any emitted value — including 0 — is a real lock-in signal and alertable with `< N` (#1628).
